videos.script:
Your phone says it is online. Your app asks the server for the week, and nothing comes back. No error, no answer, just a spinner that never stops. {{spinner}}

This lesson is about that request. A phone moves between Wi-Fi and mobile data, rides a lift, joins a café network that wants a login first. {{networks}} The system can tell you a network exists. Only a request can tell you whether your server answers.

You will run a small server that misbehaves on purpose: one route answers late, one never answers, and one fails twice before it works. {{server}} Then a client that gives up on time, {{timeout}} stops when the screen that asked goes away, and tries again without hammering the server. {{retry}}

Last, the planner's week screen. When the server is down it shows the copy it kept, and says how old it is. {{stale}} A screen that tells the truth about what it knows is the whole point.
